Jason Blakey wrote:

> Hi all - this is my first posting to the list, so please be gentle...

Hey, we're all nice here, now aren't we? ;)

>
> I've got (finished today) RedHat 6.0 (with updates) running on a 4100
> 5/466 with 512M RAM and 4 4.3G disks.  The boot up command looks like
> this...
>
> boot dkb0 -file vmlinux -flags "root=/dev/sda1"
>
> and it seems to work great - however, i've seen some crashes back to the P
> prompt during boot up...  They seem to happen after the kernel loads,
> between the "Starting CROND" and "Starting INET" rc scripts....

Humm...wierd.  Could you send me/us a full log of the boot sequence?  Not to
be a weenie, but I can't remember when I last saw a fully clean boot on my
rawhide...<smirk>

> Anyone have any ideas - i'd like to set up the bootdev_dev, boot_osflags
> and boot_file to do the work for me - but it does not seem to work...

What do you mean by "does not seem to work"?  Just that it doesn't get any
better, or that none of the settings seem to hold?  Firstly, as I so often
recommend, I'd upgrade the firmware to 5.4 - you can find it on the Compaq
web site (it's still under www.digital.com IIRC).  Let me know if you can't
find it - I'll dig up my pointer.  Second, asking a stupid question:  you are
doing it as follows, right?

P00>>> set boot_file vmlinux
P00>>> set boot_osflags root=/dev/sda1
P00>>> set bootdef_dev dkb0

If you are, and it still doesn't take it, there are some larger problems
here...but I'd rather not worry about that as it's hopefully not the case.
Lemme know - I'm always interested in rawhide-related stuff ;)

 - Pete

