Content-Type: text/plain; charset=US-ASCII
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
Content-Disposition: inline

Thanks to all on the list for your help. =20

There were a lot of great tips and suggestions.   However, the resolution =
turned out that I had to do the install of RH using FDISK (but NOT BSD =
labeling (yet!)), and then label w/ BSD style after the initial install.  =
I had been trying to do the install w/BSD labeling from the beginning.  =
After that, things went very smoothly and I now have a bootable RH 5.2 Dec =
Alpha system.  Now that I understand what my problem was, it is time to go =
to 6.0, set-up IP masquerading.........

Thanks again to all!

- Matt


