On Sat, 28 Aug 1999, Jonas Gustavsson wrote:
<snip>
>have anyone tried Wine or bochs on Alpha Linux, or more inportantly have
>anyone tried to get wine to run Alpha NT code??
A few weeks ago I tried compiling wine on my LX. It failed with some 64bit
issues. I asked in the newsgroup and they seem to be aware of it but
unsure of how to handle it. The problem seems that NT is not 64bit clean
itself but that I don't know.

>What about that VMware??, I guess there will be quite a big market for that 
>nowdays :-)
VMWare won't run on Alpha because it directly executes code from the guest
OS (and it's application). Thats exactly the difference to bochs wich
tries to emulate the guests CPU. Probably one could programm a
vmware/alpha which would be capable of running Alpha NT inside Linux or
vice versa.

